{
  "comment": [
    "Source definitions. Authority is policy: a source is promoted by a reviewed",
    "change to this file, never by discovery. A source is pinned by its id; the",
    "url is an attribute of it, so a move is a change recorded here and not a",
    "content change inferred from a redirect.",
    "transport git walks commits; transport http banks one body per poll.",
    "branch null means the collector follows whatever the remote declares as its",
    "default. pathPrefix null means the whole tree is tracked.",
    "An http endpoint is only usable as evidence if its body is stable when",
    "nothing has happened. Endpoints carrying counters - download counts, view",
    "counts - change on every poll and bank an observation that says nothing.",
    "Splice is tracked by TAGS for that reason, not by the releases endpoint."
  ],
